'''Magistar Incarnon Genesis''' is an item that is used to add [[Incarnon]] upgrades to the {{Weapon|Magistar}} or {{Weapon|Sancti Magistar}}.

==Acquisition==
*Upon completion of [[The Duviri Paradox]] and [[Angels of the Zariman]], and unlocking [[The Steel Path]], players can earn '''Magistar Incarnon Genesis''' from [[The Circuit]]'s Steel Path to place on their Magistar with the help of [[Cavalero]] in the [[Chrysalith]]. This [[Incarnon Genesis]] form grants it evolutions to a transformation and newfound strength.
*Purchased from Cavalero for {{pc|120}}, complete with the resources used in its installation. This purchase can only be made '''once'''.

==Incarnon Genesis==

===Evolutions===
*Installing the Magistar Incarnon Genesis requires 20 {{Resource|Pathos Clamp|Pathos Clamps}}, 70 {{Resource|Dracroot}}, and 150 {{Resource|Aggristone}}.
*When installed, the first Evolution tier is unlocked. The following Evolution tiers, their requirements for unlocking them, and their related perks, are shown below;
**Each challenge additionally grants '''5,000''' [[affinity]] to the weapon, affected by [[Affinity Booster]]s.

====Evolution I====
*Reach '''6x''' Combo and then [[Melee#Heavy Attack|Heavy Attack]] to activate Incarnon Form.
*Incarnon Form increases Initial Combo and Wind Up Speed
**'''+100%''' Melee Damage
**'''+30''' Initial Combo
**'''+50%''' Heavy Attack Wind Up Speed
**'''+10%''' Sprint Speed
**'''+10%''' to Bullet Jump.
*Incarnon Form lasts for '''180''' seconds and persists until [[death]].

====Evolution II====
''Unlock Challenge:'' Complete a solo mission with this weapon equipped.
*Perk 1: '''Crushing Verdict:'''
**Increase Damage by '''+100''' (Magistar) / '''+20''' (Sancti).
**With [[Channeled Abilities|Channeled Ability]] active: Increase Follow Through by '''+40%'''.
*Perk 2: '''Edge Of Justice:'''
**Increase Damage by '''+100''' (Magistar) / '''+20''' (Sancti).
**With Melee Weapon Equipped: '''+40%''' attack speed.

====Evolution III====
''Unlock Challenge:'' Activate this weapon's Incarnon form '''6''' times in a mission.
*Perk 1: '''Seismic Slam:'''
**'''+100%''' Slam Radius.
*Perk 2: '''Orokin Reach:'''
**'''+1.4''' Range.
*Perk 3: '''Swift Break:'''
**'''+30%''' Heavy Attack Wind Up Speed.

====Evolution IV====
''Unlock Challenge:'' Perform '''20''' downed Finisher attacks.
*Perk 1: '''Flashing Bleed:'''
**'''+50%''' Chance of {{D|Slash|Bleed}} on {{D|Impact}} Status Effect.
*Perk 2: '''Subtle Force:'''
**Increase Critical Chance by '''+8%'''.
**Increase Status Chance by '''+8%'''.
*Perk 3: '''Critical Parallel:'''
**Increase Critical Chance by '''+16%''' (Magistar) / '''+12%''' (Sancti).
**Increase Critical Damage Multiplier by '''+1x''' (Magistar) / '''+0.2''' (Sancti).

==Tips==
*Crushing Verdict's channeling requirement can only be met by a handful of channeled abilities that still permit melee actions:
**{{WF|Baruuk}}'s {{A|Elude}}.
**{{WF|Chroma}}'s {{A|Spectral Scream}} or {{A|Effigy}}.
**{{WF|Cyte-09}}'s {{A|Neutralize}}.
**{{WF|Ember}}'s {{A|Immolation}} when fully heated.
**{{WF|Equinox}}'s {{A|Mend & Maim|Mend}} or {{A|Mend & Maim|Maim}}.
**{{WF|Ivara}}'s {{A|Prowl}}.
**{{WF|Nyx}}'s {{A|Absorb}} with {{M|Assimilate}}.
**{{WF|Oberon}}'s {{A|Renewal}}.
**{{WF|Sevagoth}}'s {{A|Gloom}} when draining within enemy range. This is also the only ability on this list that can be transferred via the [[Helminth]]. 
*The Incarnon-form's lifesteal exclusive to {{Weapon|Sancti Magistar}} counts direct melee hits and slam radial damage (improved by Evolution III: Seismic Slam), but not status damage. High attack speed is advised to have regular healing. 
**All lifesteal on the weapon heals allies.
**Lifesteal is counted on the final damage inflicted upon a target, and is therefore reduced by enemy damage reduction, armor and resistances.
**Lifesteal does not work on object health, but will work when transferred through {{A|Tornado}}.
*Using {{WF|Titania}}'s {{A|Razorwing}} deactivates the incarnon form of melee weapons, helping you unlock Evolution III quicker.

==Known Bugs==
*Evolution IV: Flashing Bleed can proc once for every hit, and only if there is no other {{D|Slash}} proc on the hit. This makes it only 30% to 20% effective instead of the perceived 50%. 
**More than one {{D|Impact}} proc will only roll the chance once.
**A multi-proc hit with both a natural (or provided by {{A|Seeking Talons}}) {{D|Slash}} proc and an {{D|Impact}} proc will '''not''' roll Flashing Bleed at all.

* {{M|Condition Overload}} ignores damage bonuses of Crushing Verdict and Edge Of Justice as well as [[Stance]] multipliers.

* Evolution I: '''+100%''' Melee Damage as well as Evolution IV: Subtle Force and Critical Parallel affect pseudo-exalted weapons such as {{A|Landslide}}, {{A|Slash Dash}}, {{A|Shattered Lash}} and {{A|Whipclaw}}.
** {{A|Blade Storm}} is unaffected.

==Trivia==
*The Magistar's Seismic Slam evolution is only the third  bonus in the game that increases melee slam radius, the first being {{Weapon|Arca Titron|Arca Titron's}} Slam Capacitor and the second being the {{Weapon|Praedos}}'s Seismic Slam evolution. It is tied for the largest slam radius in the game with {{Weapon|Arca Titron|Arca Titron's}} heavy slam attack with 5 Slam Capacitor stacks.

